            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for electric light, then the Gujarati for to put out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ખસેડવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ખસેડવું — khaseḍvũ — \"to move, to shift\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "અમે પલંગ ખસેડીએ છીએ. — ame palaṅg khaseḍīe chīe — \"We move the bed.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ખસેડવું (khaseḍvũ) is built on the inherited khasvũ, \"to slide, move\", with a causative ending. CDIAL traces khasvũ to khasati, \"falls, slips\", a reconstructed form (CDIAL 3856)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
